Owner decision OD-DLP003-R3. Transaction ownership contract: Audit and Evidence append APIs MUST execute inside a verified caller-owned open transaction and MUST NOT issue BEGIN, COMMIT or ROLLBACK. Callers MUST prove an authorized open transaction on the injected client before invoking append methods; do not assume an arbitrary PostgreSQL client is already inside a transaction. Reuse the DLP-002 caller-owned transaction ownership contract without modifying any frozen DLP-002 implementation file. Do not call self-managing bindTaskClaimLease or releaseTaskClaimLease inside another transaction. Full atomic Task+Claim+Lease+Audit composition is OUT OF SCOPE and requires a separate owner governance decision after transaction-contract review. A failed append MUST NOT cause an unintended COMMIT; DENY, throw or failure must leave no committed ghost row for that attempt.

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R4. Immutability contract: durable Audit events and Evidence facts are append-only. Database-level immutability MUST be enforced for the disposable proof role using BOTH (1) restrictive table privileges that deny UPDATE and DELETE to the non-owner proof role used by tests, AND (2) BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE triggers that RAISE EXCEPTION fail-closed. Tests MUST prove both mechanisms. This proof MUST NOT claim protection against a PostgreSQL superuser or table owner unless those identities are separately tested and proven; unproven superuser/owner bypass remains an accepted residual boundary of the disposable proof.

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R5. Event identity, task identity, event type, governance revision and idempotency binding semantics MUST be preserved for Audit appends. Evidence facts MUST preserve evidence identity, task identity, actor reference, governance revision, evidence type and evidence ref semantics consistent with the TECP-013/TECP-016 field contracts, implemented as self-contained validation inside the new repository without mutating tecp/** sources. Conflicting reuse of an idempotency key with a mismatched binding MUST DENY, including concurrent attempts. Same-key same-binding replay MUST be idempotent. Invalid governance revision MUST DENY. Actor identity remains caller-supplied and unauthenticated; Audit/Evidence rows are NOT trusted operational evidence.

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R6. Ordering: database-issued monotonic sequence and/or DB-clock timestamps may be recorded for deterministic listing. Do not claim that sequence allocation alone proves transaction commit order unless that claim is explicitly tested. Hash-chain integrity claims are NOT authorized in this slice (TECP_DLP003_HASH_CHAIN_CLAIM = NO).

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R7. PostgreSQL must be a fresh local ephemeral cluster created only with initdb/pg_ctl, listen_addresses empty, Unix-domain socket only. Reuse the frozen disposablePgHarness without modifying it. No TCP listener, environment DATABASE_URL, existing application database, remote/staging/development/production database, Docker/remote fallback, credential read or external API. If local PostgreSQL binaries or isolation proof are unavailable, report BLOCKED and stop.

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R8. Required tests: successful Audit append and Evidence append inside a caller-owned transaction without inner BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK; mid-transaction ROLLBACK leaves no ghost Audit/Evidence rows; restrictive-privilege UPDATE/DELETE DENY; trigger UPDATE/DELETE DENY; idempotent same-key replay; conflicting-key DENY including concurrent contenders; invalid governance revision DENY; database outage fail-closed; ordering listing without untested commit-order claims; no hash-chain claim; frozen TECP regression remains PASS. All failures fail closed.

Owner decision OD-DLP003-R9. The proof remains disposable test evidence only and NON_OPERATIONAL. It is not a trusted Worker authentication surface, MCP Task/Claim/Evidence/Release action tool, multi-Cursor pilot, management dashboard, canonical schema adoption, or production control-plane readiness. Trusted Worker identity, recovery execution, Task+Claim+Lease+Audit composition, migration 057 and single-Cursor E2E remain separate future owner decisions.

